                      2. Geometric Invariants
   Let C be a smooth curve of genus one defined over K, and let ω be
a non-zero regular 1-form on C, also defined over K. We say that ω
is an invariant differential. Over K, the pair (C, ω) may be put in the
form
(1)             y 2 + a1 xy + a3 y = x3 + a2 x2 + a4 x + a6
with ω = dx/(2y + a1 x + a3 ).
Definition 2.1. The geometric invariants of the pair (C, ω) are
                      c4 = b22 − 24b4
                      c6 = −b32 + 36b2 b4 − 216b6
where b2 = a21 + 4a2 , b4 = 2a4 + a1 a3 and b6 = a23 + 4a6 .
