Proof: Let ξσ = σ(α)α−1 for σ ∈ Gal(K/K). Since ωE and ωC are
both K-rational we deduce that ξσ∗ ωE = ωE . It follows by Lemma 2.4
that ξσ is a translation. So C is the twist of E by the class of {ξσ } in
H 1 (K, E). In particular C is a torsor under E, the action µ : E × C →
C being given by
                        µ(P, Q) = α(P + α−1 Q).
It follows that E is the Jacobian of C.                                 
