  We recall from Definition 4.12 that models φ, φ0 ∈ Xn are properly
equivalent if there exists g ∈ Gn with gφ = φ0 and det(g) = 1.
Lemma 5.22. Let φ, φ0 ∈ X1 with Cφ and Cφ0 smooth curves of genus
one. Then φ and φ0 are properly equivalent if and only if πn (φ) and
πn (φ0 ) are properly equivalent.
Proof: One implication is clear from Proposition 4.7. For the con-
