The core four-row theorem has survived, but with several proof-level repairs. The strongest correction is now clear: the LLR bridge is valid here because characteristic zero rules out wild-fibre torsion, not because connected flat genus-one families are automatically cohomologically flat. I also recovered an extra sharp condition: local Hodge length \(k\) gives ternary-cubic level exactly \(k\), so the lower valuation bounds must be accompanied by “not simultaneously at the next \(4/6\) threshold.”
